</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes" data-na="Menus have one size: 32px items. Use a sheet or a page when items need more room."><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-matrix"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">Hover</th><th scope="col">Focus</th><th scope="col">Disabled</th><th scope="col">Checked / open</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Item</th>
        <td><ul class="menu menu--static" role="menu" aria-label="Default item"><li role="none"><button class="menu__item" role="menuitem" type="button">Message Nia</button></li></ul></td>
        <td><ul class="menu menu--static" role="menu" aria-label="Hovered item"><li role="none"><button class="menu__item" role="menuitem" type="button" data-state="hover">Message Nia</button></li></ul></td>
        <td><ul class="menu menu--static" role="menu" aria-label="Focused item"><li role="none"><button class="menu__item" role="menuitem" type="button" data-state="focus">Message Nia</button></li></ul></td>
        <td><ul class="menu menu--static" role="menu" aria-label="Disabled item"><li role="none"><button class="menu__item" role="menuitem" type="button" aria-disabled="true">Add to calendar</button></li></ul></td>
        <td><ul class="menu menu--static" role="menu" aria-label="Checked item"><li role="none"><button class="menu__item" role="menuitemradio" aria-checked="true" type="button">Best match</button></li></ul></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Danger item</th>
        <td><ul class="menu menu--static" role="menu" aria-label="Danger item"><li role="none"><button class="menu__item menu__item--danger" role="menuitem" type="button">Sign out</button></li></ul></td>
        <td><ul class="menu menu--static" role="menu" aria-label="Hovered danger item"><li role="none"><button class="menu__item menu__item--danger" role="menuitem" type="button" data-state="hover">Sign out</button></li></ul></td>
        <td><ul class="menu menu--static" role="menu" aria-label="Focused danger item"><li role="none"><button class="menu__item menu__item--danger" role="menuitem" type="button" data-state="focus">Sign out</button></li></ul></td>
        <td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Trigger</th>
        <td><button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false">Maya {{icon:chevron-down|icon--sm}}</button></td>
        <td><button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false" data-state="hover">Maya {{icon:chevron-down|icon--sm}}</button></td>
        <td><button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false" data-state="focus">Maya {{icon:chevron-down|icon--sm}}</button></td>
        <td><button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false" disabled>Maya {{icon:chevron-down|icon--sm}}</button></td>
        <td><button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="true" data-state="active">Maya {{icon:chevron-down|icon--sm}}</button></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>In the last column the trigger shows the open state (<code>aria-expanded="true"</code>, pressed background); keyboard focus moves to the first item when the menu opens.</p>
  <h3>Both themes</h3>
  {{themes}}<ul class="menu menu--static" role="menu" aria-label="Account menu preview"><li role="none"><button class="menu__item" role="menuitem" type="button">{{icon:user|icon--sm}}Account settings</button></li><li role="none"><button class="menu__item" role="menuitem" type="button" data-state="hover">{{icon:bell|icon--sm}}Notifications</button></li><li role="separator" class="menu__divider"></li><li role="none"><button class="menu__item menu__item--danger" role="menuitem" type="button">{{icon:log-out|icon--sm}}Sign out</button></li></ul>{{/themes}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The panel opens below the trigger, aligned to its start edge, and flips above or to the end edge when it would leave the viewport (CDK Overlay flexible positioning).</li>
    <li>Below 640px a menu with more than five items opens as a bottom sheet (the <a href="dialog.html">dialog</a> sheet layout) so items become full-width 44px targets.</li>
    <li>Item labels do not wrap; the panel grows to the longest label up to <code>min(20rem, 100vw - 32px)</code> and truncates beyond that.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p>The panel uses <code>--color-bg-surface-raised</code>, <code>--color-border-default</code> and <code>--shadow-3</code>; items use <code>--color-bg-subtle</code> on hover and focus. In dark the raised surface is grey 800, lighter than the page, so the panel reads as elevated without relying on the shadow. Danger items read <code>--color-danger-fg</code> on <code>--color-danger-bg</code> when highlighted.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3>
  <p><a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/menu-button/">APG Menu Button</a>: trigger <code>&lt;button aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded aria-controls&gt;</code>; list <code>role="menu"</code> labelled by the trigger; items <code>role="menuitem"</code>, <code>menuitemradio</code> or <code>menuitemcheckbox</code> with <code>aria-checked</code>; wrappers <code>role="none"</code>; dividers <code>role="separator"</code>. Implement with Angular CDK Menu.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><kbd>Enter</kbd>, <kbd>Space</kbd>, <kbd>↓</kbd></td><td>On the trigger: opens the menu and focuses the first item.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>↑</kbd></td><td>On the trigger: opens the menu and focuses the last item.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>↓</kbd> / <kbd>↑</kbd></td><td>Moves between items, wrapping; disabled items are focusable but inert.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Home</kbd> / <kbd>End</kbd></td><td>First / last item.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Type a letter</td><td>Moves to the next item starting with that letter.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Enter</kbd>, <kbd>Space</kbd></td><td>Activates the item and closes the menu (checkable items toggle).</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Esc</kbd></td><td>Closes the menu and returns focus to the trigger.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>Closes the menu and moves on in page order.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3>
  <p>Focus moves into the menu on open (roving focus; the item background shows focus instead of a ring) and returns to the trigger on close. Clicking outside closes it without moving focus.</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3>
  <p>The menu is labelled by its trigger (<code>aria-labelledby</code>) or an <code>aria-label</code> that names the object: "Appointment HP-1048 actions". An icon-only trigger needs <code>aria-label</code> ("More actions for HP-1048"). Shortcut hints are visible text only.</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Item on panel|--color-fg-default|--color-bg-surface-raised|4.5}}
    {{pair:Highlighted item|--color-fg-default|--color-bg-subtle|4.5}}
    {{pair:Danger item highlighted|--color-danger-fg|--color-danger-bg|4.5}}
    {{pair:Section label on panel|--color-fg-subtle|--color-bg-surface-raised|4.5}}
  </div>
  <h3>Motion</h3>
  <p>The panel scales in from 96% and fades over <code>--duration-fast</code> with <code>--ease-enter</code>; closing is instant. Reduced motion makes the entrance instant.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3>
  <p>Items are 32px tall and full width with no gaps between them; on touch-only devices and below 640px, long menus become a sheet with 44px items.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Items are verb phrases in sentence case: "Request a change", "Message Nia", "Sign out".</li>
    <li>Order by frequency; put destructive items last, after a divider.</li>
    <li>An item that opens a dialog needs no trailing "…".</li>
    <li>The trigger says what the menu is about: the person's first name for the account, "More actions" for overflow.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><ul class="menu menu--static" role="menu" aria-label="Account do"><li role="none"><button class="menu__item" role="menuitem" type="button">Account settings</button></li><li role="separator" class="menu__divider"></li><li role="none"><button class="menu__item menu__item--danger" role="menuitem" type="button">Sign out</button></li></ul></div><figcaption>Keep sign-out last in the account menu, and confirm it in the sign-out dialog.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><ul class="menu menu--static" role="menu" aria-label="Navigation dont"><li role="none"><button class="menu__item" role="menuitem" type="button">Styles</button></li><li role="none"><button class="menu__item" role="menuitem" type="button">Braiders</button></li><li role="none"><button class="menu__item" role="menuitem" type="button">Appointments</button></li></ul></div><figcaption>Hiding the primary sections behind a menu on desktop; they are top bar links.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><div class="cluster"><button class="btn" type="button">Request a change</button><button class="btn btn--link" type="button">Cancel request</button></div></div><figcaption>Two actions on the appointment card stay visible as buttons, as in the mock.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--icon" type="button" aria-label="More actions for HP-1048" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false">{{icon:more}}</button></div><figcaption>Hiding just two actions behind an overflow menu adds a step for no space saved.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{tok:Panel background|--color-bg-surface-raised}}
      {{tok:Panel border|--color-border-default}}
      {{tok:Item text|--color-fg-default}}
      {{tok:Item highlight|--color-bg-subtle}}
      {{tok:Danger item text / highlight|--color-danger-fg|--color-danger-bg}}
      {{tok:Checked mark|--color-fg-accent}}
      {{tok:Disabled item|--color-fg-disabled}}
      {{tok:Panel shadow|--shadow-3}}
      {{tok:Panel radius / item radius|--radius-md|--radius-sm}}
      {{tok:Item height|--control-height-sm}}
      {{tok:Item padding / panel padding|--space-3|--space-1}}
      {{tok:Layer|--z-dropdown}}
      {{tok:Enter motion|--duration-fast|--ease-enter}}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;div class="menu-anchor"&gt;
  &lt;button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="account-trigger"
          aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="account-menu"&gt;Maya …&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;ul class="menu" id="account-menu" role="menu" aria-labelledby="account-trigger"&gt;
    &lt;li role="none"&gt;&lt;a class="menu__item" role="menuitem" href="/settings"&gt;Account settings&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li role="separator" class="menu__divider"&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li role="none"&gt;&lt;button class="menu__item menu__item--danger" role="menuitem" type="button"&gt;Sign out&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  <table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Class / attribute</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>.menu-anchor</code></td><td>Positioning context for the panel.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.menu</code></td><td>Floating panel at <code>--z-dropdown</code>; <code>.menu--static</code> renders it in flow (docs).</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.menu__item</code></td><td>Item row; <code>.menu__item--danger</code> for destructive items.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.menu__group</code> / <code>.menu__divider</code></td><td>Section label / separator.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>aria-checked="true"</code></td><td>On <code>menuitemradio</code> / <code>menuitemcheckbox</code>: shows the check mark.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>aria-disabled="true"</code></td><td>Disabled item, still focusable.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-state="hover|focus"</code></td><td>Documentation only.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <p>Core-set component: no mock uses a menu yet. Its look comes from the mocks' kit (<code>.menu</code> in <code>docs/mocks/assets/ui.css</code>) and its likely first uses are on these screens:</p>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/style-gallery/default|top bar account link "Maya", a candidate for an account menu}}
    {{mock:dialogs/sign-out/default|the confirmation an account-menu "Sign out" opens}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed during extraction: the kit's menu had no section label or checked-item style (added <code>.menu__group</code> and <code>aria-checked</code> styling); danger items had no highlighted colour (now <code>--color-danger-bg</code>).</p>
</section>
